{"id":"41495097-341b-4ec5-b7e5-a450cf45fc23","slug":"falcon-9-block-5-dragon-in-flight-abort-test","flight":90,"name":"Falcon 9 Block 5 | Dragon In-Flight Abort Test","mission":"Crew Dragon In-Flight Abort Test","net":"2020-01-19T15:30:00Z","precision":"minute","outcome":"success","status":"Launch Successful","vehicle":"Falcon 9 Block 5","vehicleSlug":"falcon-9-block-5","family":"falcon-9","pad":"Launch Complex 39A","site":"Kennedy Space Center","orbit":"Sub","missionType":"Test Flight","crewed":false,"landings":{"attempted":0,"landed":0},"reused":true,"thumb":"https://thespacedevs-prod.nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com/media/images/255bauto255d__image_thumbnail_20240305193628.jpeg","patch":"https://thespacedevs-prod.nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com/media/mission_patch_images/dragon2520in-f_mission_patch_20210608182111.png","description":"When the Falcon 9 Block 5 rocket reaches Max-Q (maximum dynamic forces), the launch abort system of the Crew Dragon spacecraft will be triggered.\r\nThis will fire up its SuperDraco engines and propel the spacecraft and its theoretical passengers away from the launch vehicle before landing back safely in the Atlantic Ocean.\r\n\r\nThe goal of this test is to demonstrate the capacity of the spacecraft to ensure a safe return to the ground for the astronauts in the event of a launch vehicle failure.\r\n\r\nThe booster for this launch will be B1046, a thrice-flown core which was the first of the Block 5 generation. It will not attempt to land and is expected to be destroyed by the SuperDracos and aerodynamic loads.","image":{"url":"https://thespacedevs-prod.nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com/media/images/falcon_9_image_20230807133459.jpeg","thumb":"https://thespacedevs-prod.nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com/media/images/255bauto255d__image_thumbnail_20240305193628.jpeg","credit":"SpaceX","license":"CC BY-NC 2.0","generic":true},"patches":[{"name":"Dragon In-Flight Abort Test","url":"https://thespacedevs-prod.nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com/media/mission_patch_images/dragon2520in-f_mission_patch_20210608182111.png"}],"window":{"start":"2020-01-19T13:00:00Z","end":"2020-01-19T19:00:00Z"},"probability":null,"weather":null,"failReason":null,"location":{"name":"Kennedy Space Center, FL, USA","lat":28.60822681,"lon":-80.60428186,"timezone":"America/New_York"},"orbitName":"Suborbital","stages":[{"type":"Core","serial":"B1046","boosterFlight":4,"reused":true,"turnaroundDays":411.9,"landing":{"attempted":false,"success":null,"type":"Expended","location":"ATL","description":"NO attempt to recover this stage was made. The booster did not have any recovery  hardware installed."}}],"spacecraft":[{"name":"Crew Dragon C205","serial":"C205","destination":"Atlantic Ocean","crew":[]}],"payloads":[],"timeline":[],"videos":[{"title":"Crew Dragon | Launch Escape Demonstration","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mhrkdHshb3E","source":"SpaceX"}],"links":[{"title":"","url":"https://www.spacex.com/launches/crew-dragon-launch-escape-demonstration/","source":null}],"yearCount":2,"prev":{"slug":"falcon-9-block-5-starlink-2","name":"Starlink 2"},"next":{"slug":"falcon-9-block-5-starlink-3","name":"Starlink 3"}}